hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1128","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Othman bin Omar told us, Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha. H Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Ibn Shihab told me, he said: Urwah said, she said Aisha: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out in the middle of the night and prayed in the mosque, and some men led his prayer, and by morning people They talk about that, and when the third night came, the people of the mosque increased, so he went out and prayed, and they prayed with his prayer. Fourth: The mosque was incapable of being occupied by its people, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not go out to them. Then some of them started calling for prayer, and the The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until he went out for the dawn prayer, and when he finished the dawn prayer, he got up and turned to them with his face, so he testified and praised them. God praised him, then said: “As for what follows, your situation is not hidden from me, but I feared that the night prayer would be imposed on you and you would be unable to perform it.” On her authority: “This is the wording of the hadith of Al-Duraqi”"
